  "category": "adaptive-flesh",
  "description": "Calibration approaches the body as a field of forces held in a programmed balance, translating pressure into contour and rhythm.\n\nEchoing the logic of the hydrostatic skeleton, its forms emerge through the dependency of softness and constraint. Neither fixed nor freely expanded, their are systematically shaped by a programmed distribution of pressures.\n\n“In short, the form of an object is a ‘diagram of forces.’”\n D’Arcy Wentworth Thompson, On Growth and Form\n\nModelled in Zbrush and Maya, rendered in Arnold.",
